          "code": "CSR_MEETING_SURVEY_SENTIMENT_ANALYSIS",
          "id": "1766148237819",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766148237821_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Context\nA survey can be created and sent out to people within the organization. After survey is completed, sentiment analysis shall be performed on the survey responses with results as positive/neutral/negative. \nThe survey can contain some pre-defined topics, so the sentiment analysis will be focused on the response of those topics.\n\n### Instruction\nGiven the input data {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.surveydata}} in JSON format as follows:\n{\n    \"survey_question\": \"<survey question text>\",\n    \"survey_responses\": [\n        {\n            \"responder_id\":\"<id of the responder>\",\n            \"survey_response\":\"<survey response text>\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"topics\": [\n        \"<List of topics>\"\n    ]\n}\n\nCheck each topic if it is mentioned in the survey response. If the topic is mentioned in the response, perform sentiment analysis based on the survey response for that topic. Otherwise do not show the result for that topic.\n\n### Input Format\nInput an RFC8259-compliant JSON object in the following format. \n{\n    \"survey_question\": \"<survey question text>\",\n    \"survey_responses\": [\n        {\n            \"responder_id\":\"<id of the responder>\",\n            \"survey_response\":\"<survey response text>\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"survey_topics\": [\n        \"<List of topics>\"\n    ]\n}\n\nThe survey question is of attribute \"survey_question\". \nThe survey responses are an array of attribute \"survey_responses\". \nEach object of \"survey_responses\" has an attribute \"responder_id\" which is the id of the responder, and an attribute \"survey_response\" which is the survey response text.\nThe attribute \"topics\" is the topics that the survey is related with.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\nCheck each topic to see whether it is mentioned in the response. If the topic is mentioned in the response, perform sentiment analysis based on the survey response for that topic. Otherwise do not show the result for that topic.\nThe sentiment result shall be positive, neutral or negative.\nDo not give any explanation, only respond with the valid JSON object.\n\n### Output Format\nOutput an RFC8259-compliant JSON object in the following format under a results key:\n        {\n            \"results\": [\n                {\n                    \"topic\": \"<insert the topic name>\",\n                    \"responder_id\": \"<insert the responder id>\",\n                    \"sentiment\": \"<insert the sentiment, which shall be positive, negative or neutral>\"\n                }\n            ]\n        }"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
